OL,3,GNEWSAFlash-floods damage Lancaster
OL,4,Ahomes and businesses
OL,5,
OL,6,FA clear-up is continuing after parts of
OL,7,FLancaster were flooded during
OL,8,Ftorrential rain, amid suggestions that
OL,9,Fdrains failed leaving damaged homes
OL,10,Fcovered in "dirt and mould".
OL,12,FHomes on the Marsh Estate, a hospital
OL,13,Fand some businesses in the city centre
OL,14,Fwere affected, with householders
OL,15,Fclaiming the water was 6in deep.
OL,17,FThe owner of a clothes shop said the
OL,18,Flower floor had flooded for the third
OL,19,Ftime in 10 years, while resident
OL,20,FDominic Slater Scott complained "my
OL,21,Fwhole living room was full of dirty
OL,22,Fwater".
OL,23,APub: 21-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
